# Large data directories — skip traversal entirely (1.6 TB total)
# Trailing * catches version-suffixed sibling dirs too (e.g. crispresso_v2/,
# gatk_v2/) - the REF_VERSION migration (see codes/genome_versions.sh)
# creates these as siblings for some stages, not nested subdirectories, so
# an exact directory name here would silently miss them.
raw_fastq/
trimmed_fastp/
trimmed_trimmomatic/
reference*/
gatk*/
crispresso*/
mapping*/
multiqc_report/
6KAD5R5/
/assembly*/
intermediate_files/

# GenomicsDB workspace — thousands of TileDB binary segment files
gatk/trimmomatic/genomicsdb/
gatk/fastp/genomicsdb/

# Assembly pipeline intermediate/log/downloaded data (scripts in codes/assembly/ stay tracked)
codes/assembly/intermediate_files/
codes/assembly/logs/
codes/assembly/busco_downloads/
codes/assembly/*.log.info
codes/assembly/done_step*_tag

# CRISPOR Singularity container + registered genomes - large downloaded/derived
# binaries, regenerable via crispor_add_genomes.sh / crispor_add_genome_v2.sh
# (scripts themselves stay tracked). A 2.4GB .sif + three .2bit genomes ended
# up committed here once (2026-09) and blew up .git to 64GB, causing
# `git push` to die with "pack-objects died of signal 9" (OOM on login node).
codes/analysis/crispor_singularity/*.sif
codes/analysis/crispor_singularity/genomes/
*.sif
*.2bit

# IGV files — track BED features but not large binary GFF3/indices
igv_files/*.gz
igv_files/*.tbi
igv_files/*.bam
igv_files/*.bai
igv_files/*.fna
igv_files/*.fai

# Test BAMs that ended up in codes/
codes/CRISPResso/test_200.sorted.bam
codes/CRISPResso/test_200.sorted.bam.bai

# Large data files — catch any stragglers not covered by directory rules
*.bam
*.bai
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf
*.tbi
*.fastq.gz
*.fastq
*.fq.gz
*.fna
*.fa
*.fai
*.dict
*.amb
*.ann
*.bwt
*.pac
*.sa
*.zip
*.tdb
*.tar.gz
*.tar

# SLURM logs
logs/
*.out
*.err

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Temporary files
tmp/
*.tmp
